{"title":"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">2001 AMC 12 #4</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems\">2001 AMC 10 #16</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The mean of three numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> more than the least of the numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\nless than the greatest. The median of the three numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is their\nsum?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690fefbf9283c04ce95c27bbda18b61d25e7136b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 20\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 25\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 30\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the mean of the three numbers. Then the least of the numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b229a33cacafadea569f9d46582e5b82cb4de417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />\nand the greatest is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee4c397eb7460dbfe1cbee0f3f1abf9b1a8d817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. The middle of the three numbers is the median, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac4efd76d95dce2367e45a25811bc7142c1a3b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{3}[(m-10) + 5 + (m + 15)] = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"257\" height=\"37\" />, which can be solved to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c23aa72862fe70e88d22ea5ae2a03f36896eda11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />.\nHence, the sum of the three numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e007de612db41f5b314119ffb7b0ddca3dc6b13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot 10 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"132\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Say the three numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. When we arrange them in ascending order then we can assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is in the middle therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/889f56ce08684be3b2ab9914892de17686ae9594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>We can also assume that the smallest number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and the largest number of the three is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\nTherefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad16197107d7f601c390d022ab580e51626957f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x+y+z}{3} = x + 10 = z - 15\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"35\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e51f6f542011e65c0cbf2089887dc812c19348.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x+5+z}{3} = x + 10 = z - 15\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Taking up the first equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324e7930abfdf602a0cc3395b46e8f89ee6ef0a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+5+z}{3} = x + 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" /> and simplifying we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b91795981902eedeabb61935cd3c1477c7933a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z - 2x - 25 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" /> doing so for the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b4f7b78242663e73e771f8e385a3e8027bbd18d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+5+z}{3} = z - 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"153\" height=\"38\" /> we obtain the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd264590bb56ca468952690cf9319109d390e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 2z + 50 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd7374ae0bc7ddba0a0a34c0adafe5e6ab60db3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x - 2z + 50 = 2x - 4z + 100\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>when solve the above obtained equation and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b91795981902eedeabb61935cd3c1477c7933a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z - 2x - 25 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" /> we obtain the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/570c4f9f7cc5ba09e4d41ead0888f101788efae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore the sum of the three numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22ba07075527d6136409b6d2ec9d7fd19b93a10b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 + 5 + 0 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"172\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/t0UOhO9bJTo?si=MwvGzoT8Ya8uyx7n\">https://youtu.be/t0UOhO9bJTo?si=MwvGzoT8Ya8uyx7n</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12\">2001 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Pro